  "save": "Save",
  "cancel": "Cancel",
  "discardChanges": "Discard changes",
  "@discardChanges": {
    "description": "Discards the merged status sheet's unsaved answers and puts every field back to what the sheet opened with, without closing it. Distinct from cancel, which the app uses for a button that dismisses: this one stays on the sheet, which is the point \u2014 a reader who over-dragged the track wants the old value back and to carry on, not to start the whole visit again. Paired with save at the foot of that sheet and drawn in the recessive surfaceVariant beside it. Was reset, one word, renamed on instruction: reset names a mechanism where this names the consequence, and the button sits beside Save where the reader is deciding whether to keep what they just did. The cost is width \u2014 two words in a 44pt half-width button, which is why the pair is Expanded rather than sized to its labels."
  },
