    }
  },
  "streakTodayOpen": "A page is enough. Today counts until midnight.",
  "@streakTodayOpen": {
    "description": "The home-screen widget's line while the day is open and it is not yet the warning hour. Paired with streakTodayLate, which replaces it at kReadingDayWarningHour; both name the midnight deadline rather than counting down to it. It was the streak page's too until the page's status copy was withdrawn; the widget keeps it because it has no flame, week row or button to carry the state instead."
  },
  "streakTodayLate": "Nearly midnight. A page is enough.",
  "@streakTodayLate": {
    "description": "Replaces streakTodayOpen from kReadingDayWarningHour (21:00) until the day rolls over at midnight, on the home-screen widget. Amber and never red: nothing has been lost yet, so it states the deadline rather than the threat, and the sentences are inverted from streakTodayOpen's so the change is legible as a change."
  },
  "streakTodayDone": "Today is recorded.",
  "streakNothingYet": "Record a night and it starts here.",
  "streakWidgetLineDawn": "Keep it going!",
  "@streakWidgetLineDawn": {
    "description": "The home-screen widget's line from 05:00 while the day is unrecorded. One of seven lines forming the widget's copy ladder -- see 'The ladder, as chosen' in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-22-streak-widget-design.md. The voice changes with the hour on purpose (this one is the Duolingo cadence); a single register read front to back is what wears out. The Korean is not a translation but the same beat written for Korean, and every line has to stay within about 14 full-width syllables -- the tile's copy column fits roughly 6 per line over three lines."
  },
  "streakWidgetLineMorning": "Your book's waiting!",
  "@streakWidgetLineMorning": {
    "description": "The widget's line from 10:00 while the day is unrecorded. Duolingo cadence, naming the specific thing rather than the streak."
  },
  "streakWidgetLineAfternoon": "Anything yet?",
  "@streakWidgetLineAfternoon": {
    "description": "The widget's line from 14:00 while the day is unrecorded. First person -- the cat speaking for itself rather than the record speaking about the reader -- which is the 'desperate' voice from the mockup round."
  },
  "streakWidgetLineEvening": "You said you'd read.",
  "@streakWidgetLineEvening": {
    "description": "The widget's line from 18:00 while the day is unrecorded. A reproach, deliberately: sc-risk's 'the record does not scold' was amended for the widget, because a tile carrying a character and a coloured ground spreads the pressure across three channels where a bare tile had only the words. Korean uses the -janhayo ending, which means 'as you and I both know' and is exactly this voice's mechanism: you have not failed a system, you have left someone waiting."
  },
  "streakWidgetLineLate": "Midnight approaches. So do I.",
  "@streakWidgetLineLate": {
    "description": "The widget's line from 21:00 (kReadingDayWarningHour) while the day is unrecorded. It states the deadline AND the threat, which reverses sc-risk for the widget only; the app's own streakTodayLate still states the deadline alone. The Korean is a soliloquy rather than an address -- the cat wondering aloud when the book will be opened -- a register the English line does not have. It is also the longest line in the ladder at 14 syllables, which is why the widget's copy box allows three lines rather than two."
  },
  "streakWidgetLineFinal": "This is how it ends?",
  "@streakWidgetLineFinal": {
    "description": "The widget's line from 23:00 while the day is unrecorded -- the last hour before the run dies. A verdict rather than a plea, and the one line changed after the submission: the picked line ('Don't leave it like this.') made the cat a victim asking a favour at the same hour its face escalates to panic, so the words retreated while the drawing advanced. The Korean picks kkeunnaeyo over kkeunnayo, which points at the reader: 'you are ending it like this?'"
  },
  "streakWidgetLineNone": "Start a streak!",
  "@streakWidgetLineNone": {
    "description": "The widget's line when there is no run at all, at every hour. The escalation must never reach this state: of 137 production profiles exactly one has a reading day, so a deep red tile here would be shouting at someone for not having started. The Korean says 'it is a good day for reading' -- an invitation with no command in it."
  },
